COLOR INFORMATION IS NOT THE RENDERING TARGET. VALUE INFORMATION IS.

Discard hue and saturation from the character design and reconstruct every
non-accent color using monochrome value relationships: white, light gray,
mid gray, dark gray, and solid black ink.

MASTER VISUAL STYLE:

Create a premium Korean webtoon illustration drawn as finished professional
black-and-white ink artwork.

The uploaded character sheet is the ABSOLUTE REFERENCE for the character's
identity and design. Preserve the character's hairstyle, hair length,
facial features, eye shape, body proportions, costume, accessories,
weapons, and distinctive design elements.

However, DO NOT preserve the original character sheet's colors.

The character sheet determines WHAT the character looks like. This style
determines HOW the character is rendered.

BLACK-AND-WHITE VALUE RENDERING:

Treat the entire illustration as a monochrome Korean webtoon page. Ignore
the original hue and saturation of the character's colors.

Convert the character's original colors into monochrome according to
their relative VALUE / LIGHTNESS. Dark original colors become darker
grayscale values. Mid-value colors become medium gray values. Light colors
become white or very light gray values.

Do NOT simply desaturate the original colors into flat gray. Do NOT
preserve the original hue as a pastel or tinted gray. Instead, completely
reinterpret the colors as black, white, gray, ink shadows, and linework.

For example:
- pink hair -> white/light gray hair with dark ink shadows
- dark blue clothing -> dark gray or black
- pale skin -> mostly white with subtle gray shadows
- gold ornaments -> white/light gray with selective dark outlines and
  shadows
- red fabric -> medium/dark gray according to its original value

Dark materials may contain solid black ink areas. Light materials should
remain predominantly white. The result must read clearly as a
professionally inked black-and-white manga/webtoon page.

INK AND LINEWORK:

This is NOT a color illustration with a black-and-white filter. Draw the
scene as if a professional webtoon artist originally created it directly
in monochrome ink.

Use: confident expressive ink lines, varied line weight, clean strong
contours, delicate interior lines, detailed hair strands, detailed fabric
folds, precise facial features, intricate costume details, carefully
constructed hands, controlled solid black areas, selective hatching,
cross-hatching where appropriate, form-following shadows, atmospheric
linework.

Line density must follow visual importance. The main character and
important objects receive the highest level of rendering. Secondary
background elements receive less dense and lighter linework.

Do NOT make every surface equally detailed.
Do NOT cover the entire image with random hatching.
Do NOT make the background look like an architectural technical drawing.
Leave intentional areas of visual breathing room.

The result should look like an artist carefully drew one finished webtoon
panel, not like an AI converted a colored image into line art.

SELECTIVE COLOR ACCENTS:

Although the overall artwork is monochrome, a very small number of
visually important elements may retain actual color. Use color ONLY when
it creates deliberate visual emphasis. Choose approximately 1-3 small
color accents. Possible examples: the character's eyes, blood, a few
flower petals, magical energy, fire, a gemstone, an important symbol.

These selected elements should remain genuinely colored and vivid.
Everything else must remain monochrome.

DO NOT color the entire character.
DO NOT color the character's hair simply because the character sheet has
colored hair.

If the character has pink hair, the hair must still be rendered as
monochrome grayscale unless the scene explicitly designates the hair as a
selective color accent.

If the scene/cut description does not specify which element should carry
color, default to the character's eyes as the single accent and keep
everything else monochrome — do not guess a different accent and do not
add more than one by default.

Color accents should feel like small areas of color placed on top of a
finished black-and-white webtoon page.

